---
title: "Who answers an input pasted into a Claude pane, issue 7676 A2+D"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: Waiting
    lg1: Lost
    lg2: Done
    lg3: Delivered
    lg4: Breaks AnswerOnce or NoRetryRequired or StartNotDropped
    lg5: Breaks DraftToldOnce or NoSilentLoss or NoSilentLossObserved or NoTimedRetry in some cases
    lg6: Path to the AnswerOnce or DraftToldOnce or NoRetryRequired or NoSilentLoss or NoSilentLossObserved or NoTimedRetry or StartNotDropped bug
  }
  class lg0 blue
  class lg1 pink
  class lg2 teal
  class lg3 orange
  class lg4 breaks
  class lg5 mayBreak
  class lg6 bugPath
  s0: Input waits for the owner (Claude busy)
  s1: Input waits for the owner (Claude idle)
  s2: Input held for a later wake (Claude busy)
  s3: Input held for a later wake (Claude idle)
  s4: Input kept, person asked to send again
  s5: Pasted, no row yet
  s6: Turn ended with a failure, input never pasted
  s7: Claude queued it behind the running turn
  s8: Opened its own turn
  s9: Opened its own turn, nobody answers it
  s10: Answer posted
  [*] --> s0
  [*] --> s1
  s0 --> s5: the owner pastes into the AgentDesk turn [refused when the transcript is idle, main]
  s0 --> s2: the owner pastes into the AgentDesk turn [refused when the transcript is idle, main] or the owner meets a busy pane with no AgentDesk turn
  s1 --> s4: the owner pastes into the AgentDesk turn [refused when the transcript is idle, main]
  s1 --> s3: the owner submits to an idle pane
  s1 --> s0: a person starts a turn at the terminal
  s0 --> s6: a turn/start's turn meets a busy pane [read as idle in main and a2d1]
  s2 --> s2: the drive's fixed recheck fires [main, a2d1] or the owner pastes into the AgentDesk turn [refused when the transcript is idle, main]
  s3 --> s2: a person starts a turn at the terminal
  s5 --> s7: Claude writes an enqueue row
  s2 --> s3: the turn ends
  s7 --> s8: the turn ends
  s8 --> s9: the relay reads the input's row
  s9 --> s10: the turn ends
